{"type": "result", "session_id": "local-7b324a48815a4fb018be1d748ed19b785cbf90f503723139b2ec3a4d8380a8ed", "exit_code": 0, "text": "All 6 tests pass. Here's what was wrong and the fix:\n\n**Root cause** — In `slugify`, each separator character (`space`, `_`, `-`) appended a `-` to the output list. For input like `\"Hello   World\"` (three spaces), that produced three separate `-` entries → joined as `hello---world`. The existing collapses only handled exactly two hyphens (`--`) and double spaces (`  `), so a triple run left two adjacent hyphens, yielding `'hello--world'` instead of `'hello-world'`.\n\n**Fix** (in `/root/hermes-bench/.../tasks/LFM3-1.7B-Q4_K_M-q8kv-3x-20261101/tasks/LFM3-1.7B-Q4-K-M-a9e3dc/03-test-fix/r1/work/slugify.py`):\n\n```python\nimport re\n\ndef slugify(text):\n    out = []\n    for ch in text.lower():\n        if ch.isalnum():\n            out.append(ch)\n        elif ch in \" -_\":\n            out.append(\"-\")\n    result = \"\".join(out).strip(\"-\").replace(\"--\", \"-\").replace(\"  \", \" \")\n    return re.sub(r\"-{2,}\", \"-\", result)   # collapse runs of 2+ hyphens\n```\n\nAdded `import re` and replaced the bare `return result` with a `re.sub(r\"-{2,}\", \"-\", result)` that collapses any run of two or more consecutive hyphens into one. The rest (strip leading/trailing separators, double-space handling) is preserved.\n\nNo test file was touched; no third-party dependencies were added — only the standard library's `re`.", "tokens": {"input": 179634, "output": 8047, "total": 187681, "cache_read": 147065, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 132104, "timestamp": 1793541869594}
